WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.543
The engine-authentication decision, still
formally proposed, settles five positions.

2
00:00:05.543 --> 00:00:07.468
Consolidation comes first.

3
00:00:07.468 --> 00:00:12.066
Every production cutover runs in
parallel: create the Entra login,

4
00:00:12.066 --> 00:00:16.747
prove it works, disable the old one,
watch for thirty days, then drop it.

5
00:00:16.747 --> 00:00:21.112
SQL logins are eliminated, and
sa is disabled and renamed,

6
00:00:21.112 --> 00:00:24.611
with an empty break-glass
group for emergencies.

7
00:00:24.611 --> 00:00:27.889
Older versions upgrade or
carry a dated exception.

8
00:00:27.889 --> 00:00:30.751
And a per-instance record
is the proof of closure.

9
00:00:30.751 --> 00:00:34.550
The decision belongs to the
CISO: set the standard once,

10
00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:39.679
SQL authentication refused and sa
disabled everywhere in production.

11
00:00:39.679 --> 00:00:43.610
An instance that can't meet it
doesn't stay in mixed mode quietly;

12
00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.881
it goes to the authorizing official.

13
00:00:45.881 --> 00:00:47.810
Now, where all this runs.
